sonnei </td>\n   <td style=\"text-align:left;\"> Serology </td>\n   <td style=\"text-align:left;\"> <a href=\"https://doi.org/10.1186/s13071-018-2991-5\">Olayemi, 2018</a> </td>\n  </tr>\n  <tr>\n   <td style=\"text-align:right;padding-left: 2em;\" indentlevel=\"1\"> 2014 </td>\n   <td style=\"text-align:left;\"> Guinea </td>\n   <td style=\"text-align:left;\"> Praomys rostratus </td>\n   <td style=\"text-align:left;\"> Serology </td>\n   <td style=\"text-align:left;\"> <a href=\"https://zenodo.org/records/8177974\">Fichet-Calvet E, 2014</a> </td>\n  </tr>\n  <tr grouplength=\"2\"><td colspan=\"5\" style=\"border-bottom: 1px solid;\"><strong>Hylomyscus</strong></td></tr>\n<tr>\n   <td style=\"text-align:right;padding-left: 2em;\" indentlevel=\"1\"> 2016 </td>\n   <td style=\"text-align:left;\"> Nigeria </td>\n   <td style=\"text-align:left;\"> Hylomyscus pamfi </td>\n   <td style=\"text-align:left;\"> PCR </td>\n   <td style=\"text-align:left;\"> <a href=\"https://doi.org/10.1038/srep25280\">Olayemi, 2016</a> </td>\n  </tr>\n  <tr>\n   <td style=\"text-align:right;padding-left: 2em;\" indentlevel=\"1\"> 2018 </td>\n   <td style=\"text-align:left;\"> Nigeria </td>\n   <td style=\"text-align:left;\"> Hylomyscus pamfi </td>\n   <td style=\"text-align:left;\"> Serology </td>\n   <td style=\"text-align:left;\"> <a href=\"https://doi.org/10.1186/s13071-018-2991-5\">Olayemi, 2018</a> </td>\n  </tr>\n  <tr grouplength=\"1\"><td colspan=\"5\" style=\"border-bottom: 1px solid;\"><strong>Malacomys</strong></td></tr>\n<tr>\n   <td style=\"text-align:right;padding-left: 2em;\" indentlevel=\"1\"> 2021 </td>\n   <td style=\"text-align:left;\"> Sierra Leone </td>\n   <td style=\"text-align:left;\"> Malacomys edwardsi </td>\n   <td style=\"text-align:left;\"> Serology </td>\n   <td style=\"text-align:left;\"> <a href=\"https://doi.org/10.3390/biology10010028\">Bangura, 2021</a> </td>\n  </tr>\n</tbody>\n</table>\n\n`````\n:::\n:::\n\n\n## Reported human cases\n\n\n::: {.cell}\n\n:::\n\n\n![A) Reported human cases of Lassa fever, 2011 onwards. The first grey band (2013-2016) is the West African Ebola epidemic, the second (2020-) the COVID-19 pandemic, and the orange band an incomplete year of reporting. B) Predicted distribution of *Mastomys natalensis* over known endemic countries.](/lassa/images/lassa_cases_endemic.svg)\n\n::: {.callout-warning appearance=\"minimal\"}\nThe case figure is current to 2023-07-13 and needs regenerating.\n:::\n",
